englishSenses.definition:
n. The state or quality of being null and void; invalidity;
   forfeiture.
n. The state o quality of being irritant or irritating.

a. Having the quality of acting upon or affecting the nerves;
   quieting nervous excitement.
n. A nervine agent.

a. Authorized by commission, precept, or right;
   justifiable; defensible; as, the seizure of a thief is always
   warrantable by law and justice; falsehood is never warrantable.
